    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Tsung Shap was reported by Stewart Culin in Chinese Games With Dice And Dominoes (1895), describing games played by Chinese labourers in the USA. The name means disputing tens. It uses one set of 32 Chinese dominoes as a two-player fishing game, with tiles in a row and captures from the ends.',
